From: Devesh Rai <devesh.rai@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 13:31:52 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 36/37] Editors reload documents changed on disk

The schematic and board editors kept showing (and would later save over) their in-memory copy
when another program changed the files, for example an AI agent editing them through MCP.

A DOCUMENT_FILE_WATCHER polls the open files' modification times and sizes (which works on
Android's shared storage, unlike inotify), waits for a change to hold for two polls, and runs
only while the frame could take an API command.  The editor then reloads with ReloadFromDisk();
with unsaved edits it asks first (Reload / Keep My Edits).  Saving and ReloadFromDisk() take
a new baseline, so neither the editor's own writes nor a git reload are reported.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
